    "created_at": "2024-04-11T02:57:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-04-11T02:57:40Z",
    "body": "> * It specifies the structure of the user agent shadow tree.  This appears largely interoperable between implementations with the exception of the style or link element for the default summary styles: Gecko uses a link element as the first child, Chromium uses a style element as the last child, and WebKit does not use a style element (see below).  This specifies a style or link as the first child.\r\n\r\nAre these differences observable? If not, then perhaps the spec can be clearer about that, so that people understand any implementation strategy that achieves equivalent results is fine.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2048846794/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
      "+1": 0,
